{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790356027854,"sessionID":"ses_f267d730fffea74X46QHjBH9Sz","part":{"id":"prt_0d988f9aa001yTS6CzdMnaOO7y","messageID":"msg_0d9883a45001pTeMn6aGdOYvOf","sessionID":"ses_f267d730fffea74X46QHjBH9Sz","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790356027855,"sessionID":"ses_f267d730fffea74X46QHjBH9Sz","part":{"id":"prt_0d988f9c3001bK8TpibCNWlbmX","messageID":"msg_0d9883a45001pTeMn6aGdOYvOf","sessionID":"ses_f267d730fffea74X46QHjBH9Sz","type":"text","text":"The rendered star is larger than the 72×72 shape resource. I’ll scale the collision node to cover the sprite while preserving the requested shape dimensions, then test mouse dragging and releases both inside and outside `DropTarget`.","time":{"start":1790356027843,"end":1790356027846},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0f71324424899c63016ab6aa2a379087d0ba1a3b272cb63681","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790356027905,"sessionID":"ses_f267d730fffea74X46QHjBH9Sz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_W60g3RoUQVUylUfVEvIBnEv9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n@@\n [node name=\"CollisionShape\" type=\"CollisionShape2D\" parent=\".\"]\n+scale = Vector2(2.8, 2.8)\n shape = SubResource(\"RectangleShape2D_decoration\")\n*** Add File: /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n+extends SceneTree\n+\n+var reports: Array[Dictionary] = []\n+var failures: Array[String] = []\n+\n+\n+func _initialize() -> void:\n+\t_run.call_deferred()\n+\n+\n+func check(condition: bool, message: String) -> void:\n+\tif not condition:\n+\t\tfailures.append(message)\n+\t\tpush_error(message)\n+\n+\n+func wait_for_physics() -> void:\n+\tfor i in range(4):\n+\t\tawait physics_frame\n+\tawait process_frame\n+\n+\n+func move_mouse(point: Vector2) -> void:\n+\troot.warp_mouse(point)\n+\tvar event := InputEventMouseMotion.new()\n+\tevent.position = point\n+\tevent.global_position = point\n+\troot.push_input(event, true)\n+\n+\n+func click(point: Vector2, pressed: bool) -> void:\n+\tvar event := InputEventMouseButton.new()\n+\tevent.position = point\n+\tevent.global_position = point\n+\tevent.button_index = MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT\n+\tevent.pressed = pressed\n+\troot.push_input(event, true)\n+\n+\n+func _run() -> void:\n+\tvar main = load(\"res://scenes/main.tscn\").instantiate()\n+\troot.add_child(main)\n+\tcurrent_scene = main\n+\tvar draggable = main.get_node(\"SampleDraggable\")\n+\tvar target = main.get_node(\"DropTarget\")\n+\tdraggable.dropped.connect(func(item, areas): reports.append({\"item\": item, \"areas\": areas}))\n+\tcheck(draggable.initial_position == Vector2(512, 360), \"Initial position should be recorded\")\n+\tcheck(draggable.initial_scale == Vector2.ONE, \"Initial scale should be recorded\")\n+\tcheck(draggable.scale.is_zero_approx(), \"Spawn should start at zero scale\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.4).timeout\n+\tcheck(draggable.scale.is_equal_approx(draggable.initial_scale), \"Spawn should restore initial scale\")\n+\tvar sprite: Sprite2D = draggable.get_node(\"Sprite\")\n+\tvar collider: CollisionShape2D = draggable.get_node(\"CollisionShape\")\n+\tcheck(collider.shape.size == Vector2(72, 72), \"Collision shape should remain 72x72\")\n+\tvar collider_bounds := Rect2(-collider.shape.size * collider.scale / 2, collider.shape.size * collider.scale)\n+\tvar sprite_bounds := Rect2(sprite.get_rect().position * sprite.scale, sprite.get_rect().size * sprite.scale)\n+\tcheck(collider_bounds.encloses(sprite_bounds), \"Collision bounds should cover the scaled sprite\")\n+\n+\t# Press near an outer star point to verify the full sprite is pickable.\n+\tmove_mouse(draggable.global_position + Vector2(0, -75))\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tclick(draggable.global_position + Vector2(0, -75), true)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(draggable.dragging, \"Mouse press on the outer star should begin dragging\")\n+\tmove_mouse(target.global_position)\n+\tvar distance_before: float = draggable.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(draggable.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position) < distance_before, \"Dragging should move toward the mouse\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.5).timeout\n+\tcheck(draggable.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position) < 1.0, \"Dragging should converge on the mouse\")\n+\tclick(target.global_position, false)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(not draggable.dragging, \"Release should stop dragging\")\n+\tcheck(reports.size() == 1, \"Valid drop should emit exactly one report\")\n+\tif reports.size() == 1:\n+\t\tcheck(reports[0].item == draggable, \"Drop report should contain the draggable\")\n+\t\tcheck(reports[0].areas.has(target), \"Drop report should contain the overlapping target\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.4).timeout\n+\tcheck(is_instance_valid(draggable), \"Valid drop should keep the decoration alive\")\n+\tif not is_instance_valid(draggable):\n+\t\tquit(1)\n+\t\treturn\n+\n+\t# An unrelated layer-2 area must not be accepted as a DropTarget.\n+\tvar unrelated := Area2D.new()\n+\tunrelated.name = \"OtherArea\"\n+\tunrelated.collision_layer = 2\n+\tunrelated.position = Vector2(850, 450)\n+\tvar unrelated_shape := CollisionShape2D.new()\n+\tvar rectangle := RectangleShape2D.new()\n+\trectangle.size = Vector2(140, 140)\n+\tunrelated_shape.shape = rectangle\n+\tunrelated.add_child(unrelated_shape)\n+\tmain.add_child(unrelated)\n+\tmove_mouse(draggable.global_position)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tclick(draggable.global_position, true)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(draggable.dragging, \"A validly dropped decoration should be draggable again\")\n+\tmove_mouse(unrelated.global_position)\n+\tawait create_timer(0.6).timeout\n+\t# Release far from the sprite to check the global _input handler.\n+\tmove_mouse(Vector2(1100, 600))\n+\tclick(Vector2(1100, 600), false)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(reports.size() == 2, \"Invalid drop should emit exactly one additional report\")\n+\tif reports.size() == 2:\n+\t\tcheck(reports[1].areas.has(unrelated), \"Invalid drop should report other overlapping areas\")\n+\t\tcheck(not reports[1].areas.has(target), \"Invalid drop should not report the distant target\")\n+\tcheck(not draggable.dragging, \"Release away from the sprite should stop dragging\")\n+\tcheck(not draggable.input_pickable, \"Destructing decoration should stop accepting clicks\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.3).timeout\n+\tcheck(not is_instance_valid(draggable), \"Invalid drop should shrink and free the decoration\")\n+\tif failures.is_empty():\n+\t\tprint(\"PASS: spawn, collision coverage, mouse picking, smooth dragging, drop reports, valid retention, invalid destruction\")\n+\tquit(0 if failures.is_empty() else 1)\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\nA workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n+++ /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n@@ -17,7 +17,8 @@\n texture = ExtResource(\"2_star\")\n scale = Vector2(0.58, 0.58)\n \n [node name=\"CollisionShape\" type=\"CollisionShape2D\" parent=\".\"]\n+scale = Vector2(2.8, 2.8)\n shape = SubResource(\"RectangleShape2D_decoration\")\n \n [connection signal=\"input_event\" from=\".\" to=\".\" method=\"_on_input_event\"]\n\nIndex: /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n+++ /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@\n+extends SceneTree\n+\n+var reports: Array[Dictionary] = []\n+var failures: Array[String] = []\n+\n+\n+func _initialize() -> void:\n+\t_run.call_deferred()\n+\n+\n+func check(condition: bool, message: String) -> void:\n+\tif not condition:\n+\t\tfailures.append(message)\n+\t\tpush_error(message)\n+\n+\n+func wait_for_physics() -> void:\n+\tfor i in range(4):\n+\t\tawait physics_frame\n+\tawait process_frame\n+\n+\n+func move_mouse(point: Vector2) -> void:\n+\troot.warp_mouse(point)\n+\tvar event := InputEventMouseMotion.new()\n+\tevent.position = point\n+\tevent.global_position = point\n+\troot.push_input(event, true)\n+\n+\n+func click(point: Vector2, pressed: bool) -> void:\n+\tvar event := InputEventMouseButton.new()\n+\tevent.position = point\n+\tevent.global_position = point\n+\tevent.button_index = MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT\n+\tevent.pressed = pressed\n+\troot.push_input(event, true)\n+\n+\n+func _run() -> void:\n+\tvar main = load(\"res://scenes/main.tscn\").instantiate()\n+\troot.add_child(main)\n+\tcurrent_scene = main\n+\tvar draggable = main.get_node(\"SampleDraggable\")\n+\tvar target = main.get_node(\"DropTarget\")\n+\tdraggable.dropped.connect(func(item, areas): reports.append({\"item\": item, \"areas\": areas}))\n+\tcheck(draggable.initial_position == Vector2(512, 360), \"Initial position should be recorded\")\n+\tcheck(draggable.initial_scale == Vector2.ONE, \"Initial scale should be recorded\")\n+\tcheck(draggable.scale.is_zero_approx(), \"Spawn should start at zero scale\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.4).timeout\n+\tcheck(draggable.scale.is_equal_approx(draggable.initial_scale), \"Spawn should restore initial scale\")\n+\tvar sprite: Sprite2D = draggable.get_node(\"Sprite\")\n+\tvar collider: CollisionShape2D = draggable.get_node(\"CollisionShape\")\n+\tcheck(collider.shape.size == Vector2(72, 72), \"Collision shape should remain 72x72\")\n+\tvar collider_bounds := Rect2(-collider.shape.size * collider.scale / 2, collider.shape.size * collider.scale)\n+\tvar sprite_bounds := Rect2(sprite.get_rect().position * sprite.scale, sprite.get_rect().size * sprite.scale)\n+\tcheck(collider_bounds.encloses(sprite_bounds), \"Collision bounds should cover the scaled sprite\")\n+\n+\t# Press near an outer star point to verify the full sprite is pickable.\n+\tmove_mouse(draggable.global_position + Vector2(0, -75))\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tclick(draggable.global_position + Vector2(0, -75), true)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(draggable.dragging, \"Mouse press on the outer star should begin dragging\")\n+\tmove_mouse(target.global_position)\n+\tvar distance_before: float = draggable.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(draggable.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position) < distance_before, \"Dragging should move toward the mouse\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.5).timeout\n+\tcheck(draggable.global_position.distance_to(target.global_position) < 1.0, \"Dragging should converge on the mouse\")\n+\tclick(target.global_position, false)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(not draggable.dragging, \"Release should stop dragging\")\n+\tcheck(reports.size() == 1, \"Valid drop should emit exactly one report\")\n+\tif reports.size() == 1:\n+\t\tcheck(reports[0].item == draggable, \"Drop report should contain the draggable\")\n+\t\tcheck(reports[0].areas.has(target), \"Drop report should contain the overlapping target\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.4).timeout\n+\tcheck(is_instance_valid(draggable), \"Valid drop should keep the decoration alive\")\n+\tif not is_instance_valid(draggable):\n+\t\tquit(1)\n+\t\treturn\n+\n+\t# An unrelated layer-2 area must not be accepted as a DropTarget.\n+\tvar unrelated := Area2D.new()\n+\tunrelated.name = \"OtherArea\"\n+\tunrelated.collision_layer = 2\n+\tunrelated.position = Vector2(850, 450)\n+\tvar unrelated_shape := CollisionShape2D.new()\n+\tvar rectangle := RectangleShape2D.new()\n+\trectangle.size = Vector2(140, 140)\n+\tunrelated_shape.shape = rectangle\n+\tunrelated.add_child(unrelated_shape)\n+\tmain.add_child(unrelated)\n+\tmove_mouse(draggable.global_position)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tclick(draggable.global_position, true)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(draggable.dragging, \"A validly dropped decoration should be draggable again\")\n+\tmove_mouse(unrelated.global_position)\n+\tawait create_timer(0.6).timeout\n+\t# Release far from the sprite to check the global _input handler.\n+\tmove_mouse(Vector2(1100, 600))\n+\tclick(Vector2(1100, 600), false)\n+\tawait wait_for_physics()\n+\tcheck(reports.size() == 2, \"Invalid drop should emit exactly one additional report\")\n+\tif reports.size() == 2:\n+\t\tcheck(reports[1].areas.has(unrelated), \"Invalid drop should report other overlapping areas\")\n+\t\tcheck(not reports[1].areas.has(target), \"Invalid drop should not report the distant target\")\n+\tcheck(not draggable.dragging, \"Release away from the sprite should stop dragging\")\n+\tcheck(not draggable.input_pickable, \"Destructing decoration should stop accepting clicks\")\n+\tawait create_timer(0.3).timeout\n+\tcheck(not is_instance_valid(draggable), \"Invalid drop should shrink and free the decoration\")\n+\tif failures.is_empty():\n+\t\tprint(\"PASS: spawn, collision coverage, mouse picking, smooth dragging, drop reports, valid retention, invalid destruction\")\n+\tquit(0 if failures.is_empty() else 1)\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn","relativePath":"workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n+++ /workspace/scenes/draggable.tscn\n@@ -17,7 +17,8 @@\n texture = ExtResource(\"2_star\")\n scale = Vector2(0.58, 0.58)\n \n [node name=\"CollisionShape\" type=\"CollisionShape2D\" parent=\".\"]\n+scale = Vector2(2.8, 2.8)\n shape = SubResource(\"RectangleShape2D_decoration\")\n \n [connection signal=\"input_event\" from=\".\" to=\".\" method=\"_on_input_event\"]\n","additions":1,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd","relativePath":"workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n+++ /workspace/.godot/verify_draggable.gd\n@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@\n+extends SceneTree\n+\n+var reports: Array[Dictionary] = []\n+var failures: Array[String] = []\n+\n+\n+func _initialize() -> void:\n+\t_run.call_deferred()\n+\n+\n+func check(condition: bool, message: String) -> void:\n+\tif not condition:\n+\t\tfailures.append(message)\n+\t\tpush_error(message)\n+\n+\n+func wait_for_physics() -> void:\n+\tfor i in range(4):\n+\t\tawait physics_frame\n+\tawait process_frame\n+\n+\n+func move_mouse(point: Vector2) -> void:\n+\troot.warp_mouse(point)\n+\tvar event := InputEventMouseMotion.new()\n+\tevent.position = point\n+\tevent.global_position = point\n+\troot.push_input(event, true)\n+\n+\n+func click(point: Vector2, pressed: bool) -> void:\n+\tvar event := InputEventMouseButton